# Always Push Changes

After finishing implementation for a user request (or when the user asks to save/ship work):

1. Commit the relevant files for that request (do not mix unrelated WIP).
2. **Always push** to the remote (`git push -u origin HEAD` if upstream is missing).
3. Do not wait to be asked again to push — pushing is part of completing the work.
4. Still never force-push to main/master unless the user explicitly requests it.
5. Still never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens).
